WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.049 --> 00:00:05.370
Speaker 1: Let's hear from people in the audience
on this slightly early Friday type show, because

00:00:05.370 --> 00:00:07.440
the week is a little bit different this week.

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:12.810
We take calls via discord at David Pakman
dot com slash discord.

00:00:12.810 --> 00:00:16.309
And we're going to start today with Alex from
California.

00:00:16.309 --> 00:00:17.369
Alex, welcome.

00:00:17.369 --> 00:00:18.369
What's on your mind today?

00:00:18.369 --> 00:00:19.369
Speaker 2: Hey, David.

00:00:19.369 --> 00:00:20.480
Speaker 1: Can you hear me?

00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:21.769
I can hear you fine.

00:00:21.769 --> 00:00:22.769
Speaker 2: Nice.

00:00:22.769 --> 00:00:29.230
So when it comes to, like, elections and how
people vote, it really seems like it comes

00:00:29.230 --> 00:00:33.399
down to the economy than anything else.

00:00:33.399 --> 00:00:38.500
Like you have things like Roe v Wade or like
gay marriage be overturned.

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:44.570
But if there is like a recession in that same
year, it feels like they'll vote on the recession

00:00:44.570 --> 00:00:47.920
and say, oh, Democrats ruined the economy.

00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:50.239
Who cares about these, like civil rights issues?

00:00:50.239 --> 00:00:51.239
Yeah.

00:00:51.239 --> 00:00:52.239
What do you think about that?

00:00:52.239 --> 00:00:53.940
Speaker 1: I completely agree.

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:58.980
The perception of how the economy is doing,
even if, number one, people's perception is

00:00:58.980 --> 00:01:00.170
wrong.

00:01:00.170 --> 00:01:05.080
And number two, it doesn't really have much
to do with the president.

00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:11.860
Both are hugely influential in how people
vote.

00:01:11.860 --> 00:01:16.080
And this is why things are suddenly looking
much better for Democrats, even though I don't

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:17.890
think it really has much to do with Joe Biden.

00:01:17.890 --> 00:01:20.440
There was this blockbuster jobs report in
July.

00:01:20.440 --> 00:01:23.880
Wages are up, inflation is down, gas prices
are down, etc..

00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:28.690
It has very little to do with Joe Biden, but
it seems to be helping Democrats very much

00:01:28.690 --> 00:01:30.130
in terms of the outlook for November.

00:01:30.130 --> 00:01:34.520
So, yes, it's the economy, stupid, was the
phrase James Carville came up with.

00:01:34.520 --> 00:01:40.250
And it it is more like it is the perception
of the economy, regardless of whether it's

00:01:40.250 --> 00:01:41.250
accurate.

00:01:41.250 --> 00:01:42.330
Speaker 2: Okay.

00:01:42.330 --> 00:01:46.620
So let's say I've been here a lot of like
recession warnings coming up.

00:01:46.620 --> 00:01:49.830
They say there's going to be like a recession
in like 2024.

00:01:49.830 --> 00:01:51.200
Let's say there is.

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:52.200
Yep.

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:58.140
So is that going to be the determining factor
whether or not like Joe Biden loses the election,

00:01:58.140 --> 00:02:04.980
even though like Democrat, the Republican
agenda is like has really awful things like

00:02:04.980 --> 00:02:07.890
to like to do or how or what to do.

00:02:07.890 --> 00:02:09.570
Speaker 1: So I don't know.

00:02:09.570 --> 00:02:12.880
You're saying if there is a recession or you're
saying there won't be one?

00:02:12.880 --> 00:02:17.530
Speaker 2: Yeah, no, I'm saying if there is
a recession, that's pretty much a guaranteed

00:02:17.530 --> 00:02:20.550
loss for like Joe Biden if he if he decides
to run.

00:02:20.550 --> 00:02:21.550
Yeah.

00:02:21.550 --> 00:02:24.850
Speaker 1: I think if at the time if I think
if Joe Biden runs for reelection and there

00:02:24.850 --> 00:02:30.620
is a very clear recession in September and
October of 2024, I think Biden definitely

00:02:30.620 --> 00:02:31.620
loses.

00:02:31.620 --> 00:02:32.620
That's so far off.

00:02:32.620 --> 00:02:37.530
And remember, people have been predicting
imminent recession since 2015 and it hasn't

00:02:37.530 --> 00:02:38.530
really happened.

00:02:38.530 --> 00:02:43.170
I mean, you could argue technically we just
were in one because GDP went down very, very

00:02:43.170 --> 00:02:44.810
slightly last quarter.

00:02:44.810 --> 00:02:47.850
But when you look at every other indicator,
it's really hard to make that case.

00:02:47.850 --> 00:02:48.930
But let's wait and see.

00:02:48.930 --> 00:02:49.930
I agree with you, though.

00:02:49.930 --> 00:02:53.460
If there is really a recession, it's going
to be bad for Joe Biden if he's on the on

00:02:53.460 --> 00:02:58.880
the ticket.

00:02:58.880 --> 00:03:15.150
Speaker 2: All right.

00:03:15.150 --> 00:03:40.950
That's it.

00:03:40.950 --> 00:03:53.239
And thank you for taking my call.

00:03:53.239 --> 00:03:58.950
Speaker 1: Thank you.

00:03:58.950 --> 00:04:01.800
Appreciate it.

00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:10.130
Very, very good questions.

